ogether  and it usually comes from venom himself  more often than not SIF Parker and Brock  are on the same team it's because one of  Venom's own spawn is up to no good  like the insane and powerful villain  Cletus Kasady better known as carnage  when I get out of here and I will  there's gonna be Cara Nature  venneman Spidey famously teamed up  against the villainous symbiotes along  with other Marvel heroes in the 1993  event maximum carnage a hugely popular  storyline that inspired the classic  16-bit video game of the same name there  is a good reason why they had to team up  to physically carnage is more powerful  than spider-man and venom combined and  even more durable among other things the  villain has survived being beheaded as  well as being dragged into space and  ripped in half  even worse Cassidy was already a  convicted serial killer before he got  superpowers when his cellmate Eddie  Brock escaped from prison a scrap of the  symbiote was left behind then a  terrifying new villain was born in that  respect carnage can be thought of as  Venom's son but the symbiotes clearly  don't have the same warm fuzzy feelings  the rest of us have towards family still  the fact that venom chose to stay on  Team Spidey when he had to choose  between siding with Peter Parker or  teaming up with his own spawn says a  whole lot about his complicated  relationship with spider-man it's clear  the Venom symbiote has complicated  feelings towards Peter Parker but it's  also clear that those complex feelings  are a two-way street  Venom's place in the Marvel Universe is  always cycling between antihero and  full-on villain he can spend time as a  less forgiving crime fighter as he did  in a series of solo titles that started  in 1993 with venom lethal protector but  cut to 10 years later in 2003 venom and  he's right back to eating people for fun  and yet in spite of Venom's  unpredictability and his shifting  loyalties  spider-man never gets proactive about  shutting him d