l venom  comes close to killing Miles the younger  spider-man manages to temporarily  incapacitate the symbiote which gives  Brock a chance to take over Eddie thanks  miles and tries to explain what happened  but miles doesn't give him the chance  Miles understandably presses the attack  against Eddie and venom is forced to  fight back while Miles has never met  Eddie Brock before that issue he isn't a  stranger to symbiotes back in his home  universe his life was thrown into  disarray by that world's version of  venom in 2013 during a story  appropriately titled venom war venom  nearly killed Miles his father and his  mother died as a result of the conflict  with that kind of history it's easy to  see why Miles wouldn't be inclined to  give Eddie the benefit of the doubt once  he was attacked  eventually in true Marvel team-up  fashion the fight led to miles and Eddie  working together for the next few issues  time will tell what happens next time  these two fan favorites cross paths  Marvel has been putting out issues of  what if on and off since 1977 giving  readers the chance to experience what  stories would be like if they worked out  differently usually if the answer is  that things would be pretty bad but  1989's what if number four takes things  to the next level the question this time  around is what if the alien had  possessed spider-man and things wind up  a whole lot worse for everyone including  both Peter Parker and the symbiote the  Venom symbiote of what if number four  never develops the same emotional  attachment to Peter Parker as the main  continuities venom does instead it feeds  on its host like a vampire  draining peter's youth and vitality in  the process once Parker's lifeforce is  spent  the symbiote starts looking for a bigger  meal and chooses the Hulk as his next  host it interrupts the massive battle  between the Hulk and the Avengers that  readers had originally seen in  Incredible Hulk number 300 and bonds  with the green Goliath as he does Peter  Parker's body is revealed to have been  prematurely aged leaving him as a  withered husk Peter dies not long after  and the Avengers pursue the venom  infected Hulk until the symbiote trades  up once again leaving the Hulk's body  for Thor's the heroes finally  incapacitate venom by getting help from  the inhuman leader Black Bolt whose  deafening scream forces the symbiote  from Thor's body and destroys Mount  Rushmore in the process before the  assembled heroes can banish the symbiote  to another dimension the black cat kills  it in revenge for Parker's death all  things considered it's a much less happy  ending than we got in the regular comics  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the MCU we're coming soon subscribe to  our YouTube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one  [Music]

